VERDICT
FAIL. Contract revision 11 closes most inspected architecture findings, but two prior P1 request/version-identity findings remain contradicted by the implementation. PASS is therefore unavailable. The pass/fail decision was reached before a full lower-severity rescan, per the bounded-triage instruction.

P1 FINDINGS

1. Prior P1-1 is not closed in the actual frame path: a below-selection frame returns PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED, not PROTOCOL_DOWNGRADE.

Contract evidence: docs/spec/SMP1.md section 2 says every later frame is checked against the selection, a frame below it answers PROTOCOL_DOWNGRADE, and a frame above it answers PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED. Section 9 repeats that precedence.

Implementation evidence: crates/sley-protocol/src/lib.rs, ProtocolFrame::validate, rejects every protocol_version unequal to the crate constant PROTOCOL_VERSION with VersionUnsupported. decode_frame invokes ProtocolFrame::from_payload, which invokes validate, before Server::dispatch can call SelectedProfile::check_claim. Therefore a crafted frame carrying version 0 is rejected as 40000 PROTOCOL_VERSION_UNSUPPORTED at decode, and the contractually required 40004 PROTOCOL_DOWNGRADE branch in check_claim is unreachable through the server. The comment in server.rs that dispatch applies check_claim does not repair the earlier decoder precedence.

Required closure: make the decoded request reach one selection-aware claim check that distinguishes below from above, and pin both wire cases; or change the contract and threat disposition consistently. The current contract claim and current server behavior cannot both freeze.

2. Prior P1-2 is only partially closed: session-less request identifiers remain undefined and contradict the stated zero sentinel.

Contract evidence: docs/spec/SMP1.md section 3 defines 0 as the pre-session sentinel, says it is carried by hello frames and allowed on session.open without consuming the sequence, and sets in-session identifiers to start at 1. The same section separately permits session-less workspace.create and exchange.import on the genesis path, but gives neither method an identifier rule, scope, replay rule, or required sentinel value.

Implementation evidence: crates/sley-protocol/src/server.rs dispatches session.open before registry admission and dispatches the two headless genesis methods without RequestRegistry admission. crates/sley-protocol/src/server_tests.rs deliberately sends session.open with request identifiers 1, 99, and 100, sends session-less workspace.create with 2, and session-less exchange.import with 1. ProtocolFrame::validate constrains request_id=0 only for hello frames. Thus the implementation accepts arbitrary unscoped request identifiers on all three session-less request paths while the contract calls 0 the pre-session sentinel and never defines the nonzero space.

Required closure: freeze one exact rule for all session-less requests (recommended: request_id=0 with method/body identity or owner idempotence handling replay), or define a separate connection/pre-session sequence and enforce it. Add tests for session.open plus both genesis exemptions. The current text does not close T46 at the session-less boundary.

